      "message": "[error] Line 937: 🔴 If `onDisconnected` or `onError` is delivered before `onOpened`, `videoParams.camera` is still null, so this `isCurrent` check is false and `listener.onError()` is skipped. That leaves `isCapturing`/`pendingStartCodec` set and the encoder/surfaces may remain allocated, with no recovery path. Use the open-attempt generation (or explicitly track the pending camera) to handle failures before `onOpened`, while still rejecting stale attempts.",
